From 3900730571cfa011c59cd10e53af42c0e231237f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UTMapp-bot <noreply@getutm.app>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:59:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] gpoll: Only check fd_sets for descriptors that were added
 to them

Since the fd_sets are sized from the highest descriptor that has
G_IO_IN, G_IO_OUT or G_IO_PRI set, a higher descriptor polled for none
of them (a source that only watches for G_IO_HUP or G_IO_ERR) is past
the end of the sets. FD_ISSET() on it reads out of bounds, now that
_DARWIN_UNLIMITED_SELECT turns off the libc check that used to trap.

Skip descriptors without those events when collecting revents; select()
cannot report anything for them anyway.
---
 glib/gpoll.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/glib/gpoll.c b/glib/gpoll.c
index 293e711..366d8fc 100644
--- a/glib/gpoll.c
+++ b/glib/gpoll.c
@@ -619,7 +619,8 @@ g_poll (GPollFD *fds,
     for (f = fds; f < f_end; ++f)
       {
         f->revents = 0;
-        if (f->fd >= 0)
+        /* The sets only cover descriptors that were added to them. */
+        if (f->fd >= 0 && (f->events & poll_events))
           {
             if (FD_ISSET (f->fd, rset))
               f->revents |= G_IO_IN;
